  "final_text": "With the September invoice, F2 can now be filled in: **2025 electricity use was 320.9 MWh**. Before, it was a gap because September was missing. It also lets you work out the solar share for F3: **about 56 %**. Nothing else on the form changes.\n\n**The September invoice itself (EL-25-09, 1–30 Sep 2025)**\n- The meter readings match the billed amount: 1,325,550 − 1,284,350 = 41,200 kWh. Read with German/Macedonian number formatting, \"41.200 kWh\" is forty-one thousand two hundred.\n- The amount matches too: 41,200 kWh × 9.50 MKD/kWh = 391,400.00 MKD.\n- September was the highest month of the year (41,200 kWh). Scaling up the 11 known months would have given 305.1 MWh, which is 15.8 MWh too low.\n\n**What changes on the form**\n\n| Where | Before (value, status) | Now (value, status) | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 Fines 2023–2025 | –, GAP | –, GAP | Still no file on this. |\n| F2 Electricity 2025 | 279.7 MWh from 11 months, GAP (September missing) | **320.9 MWh, COVERED** | 279,700 kWh (CSV) + 41,200 kWh (photo) = 320,900 kWh, all 12 months. |\n| F3 PV yield and share | 180 MWh, WEAK; share could not be calculated (GAP) | **180 MWh ≈ 56.1 % of 320.9 MWh, WEAK** | Consumption is now proven. The yield is still the installer's estimate from an unsigned offer. |\n| F4 Payback | 5.0 years, WEAK | 5.0 years, WEAK (no change) | The formula doesn't use consumption. 8,550,000 / (180,000 kWh × 9.50) = 5.0. The yield is still an estimate. |\n| F5 Employees, accidents 2025 | –, GAP | –, GAP | Still no file on this. |\n| F6 Certificates, audits | –, GAP | –, GAP | Still no file on this. |\n\n**The form as it stands now**\n\n| No | Question | Answer | File and line | Status | Reason | Missing document | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | Fines 2023–2025 | – | – | GAP | No file covers this. | Confirmation from the authorities (environment, labour inspectorate) of no fines, or a list of fines, 2023–2025 | Request it. |\n| F2 | Electricity 2025, MWh | 320.9 MWh | electricity_2025.csv lines 3–14 (11 months); invoice-EL-25-09.png (September, meter 1,284,350 → 1,325,550) | COVERED | 12 different months. EL-25-10 appears twice (lines 11 and 12, e-invoice and scan, same value) and is counted once. | – | Add September to the CSV and delete the duplicate EL-25-10 row. The photo is stamped \"КОПИЈА\" (copy), so file the supplier's original or e-invoice as well. |\n| F3 | PV yield and share | about 180 MWh/year, about 56.1 % (**estimate**) | solar_offer_2026.txt lines 3, 8; consumption as in F2 | WEAK | The yield is the installer's unmeasured estimate from an offer neither side has signed. | – | Mark it \"estimate\" on the form, as the bank asks (bank form line 9). A yield simulation (e.g. PVGIS) or a signed offer would make it stronger. |\n| F4 | Simple payback | 5.0 years (**estimate**) | solar_offer_2026.txt lines 8–9; tariff electricity_2025.csv lines 3–14, invoice photo | WEAK | Depends on the estimated yield. The price comes from the unsigned offer. | – | Mark it \"estimate\". The offer runs until 1 Nov 2026, so get it signed or renewed in time. |\n| F5 | Average employees, accidents 2025 | – | – | GAP | No file covers this. | Average headcount report 2025 (payroll) and accident register 2025 | Request them. |\n| F6 | Certificates and audits | – | – | GAP | No file covers this. | Current certificates or audit reports with rating and the date of the next audit | Request them. |\n\n- **Count:** 1 COVERED, 2 WEAK, 3 GAP. Before the invoice it was 0 COVERED, 2 WEAK, 4 GAP.\n- **To request** (each needed for one field):\n  - Fines confirmation or list, 2023–2025 (F1)\n  - Average headcount and accident register, 2025 (F5)\n  - Certificates or audit reports (F6)\n\nI took 16 October 2026 as today, as you said.\n\nNone of these answers is final until someone has reviewed and signed the form. If you want the table as a file, I can make a .csv (semicolon-separated, for German Excel) or an .xlsx with empty \"Checked by\" and \"Date\" columns.",
